 [:option {:value "2007932"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/665"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Super-Heavyweight, Greco-Roman (≤130 kg), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "15 August 2016"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/902"} "Arena Carioca 2, Parque Olímpico da Barra, Barra da Tijuca, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/355726"} "19 from 19 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single elimination tournament. Competitors losing to the finalists entered repechage tournament for bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The five-time World champion, Cuban legend " [:a {:href "/athletes/107601"} "Mijaín López"] " entered the Rio Olympics looking for his third Olympic gold medal. Standing in his way was his rival, Turkey’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/117225"} "Riza Kayaalp"] ", the 2015 World champion who beat López for gold in Las Vegas for the World title the previous year. After that, " [:a {:href "/athletes/121782"} "Heiki Nabi"] " of Estonia, the 2012 Olympic silver medalist, who captured his first World title a decade previous in 2006, and a second in 2013 (along with a 2014 World bronze) was looking for a spot on the podium."] "\n\n" [:p {} "En route to the final round, López and Kayaalp dominated each of their first three Olympic matches with both not allowing an opponent a single point on them. All three of Kayaalp’s preliminary matches ended earlier than the allotted time – two were won by technical fall, and one by him pinning his opponent just after the first minute. López defeated " [:a {:href "/athletes/135829"} "Sergey Semyonov"] " of Russia in the semi-finals by a score of 3-0, while Kayaalp beat " [:a {:href "/athletes/134255"} "Eduard Popp"] " of Germany 8-0."] "\n\n" [:p {} "And in what was the third straight year that López and Kayaalp have met in a final round of a major international tournament, they faced off for Olympic gold in Rio in a very chippy match. López beat Kayaalp 6-0, to became just the third wrestler to win three Olympic gold medals in Greco-Roman joining legend Soviet/Russian wrestler " [:a {:href "/athletes/59868"} "Aleksandr Karelin"] " as the only two to win all three Greco golds consecutively. The win also put López in a tie for most wrestling medals all-time across all disciplines."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The bronze medals went to Azerbaijan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/132628"} "Sabah Şəriəti"] " and Russia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/135829"} "Sergey Semyonov"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points Received", :class "footnote"} "TPR"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/107601"} "Mijaín López"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CUB"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CUB.png"}] "CUB"]] [:td {} "12"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "16"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :sty